      "text": "Robinette developed as a coal mining community in the Guyandotte River valley during the late nineteenth and early twentieth centuries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/robinette_west_virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Chesapeake and Ohio Railway provided essential transportation for coal extracted from the region, helping form the community of Robinette.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/robinette_west_virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Buffalo Creek Road serves as the primary route through Robinette, following the path of the creek valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
